% ============================================================================
% syllable-blending.query.adj — a worked recall over the literacy
% syllable-blending library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what word do the
% syllables 'lap' and 'top' blend into?": it states no linguistics fact — it
% only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine
% resolves each `?` against the `syllable_blending` row and returns the
% blended word + the table's source/locator/trust. The second query runs the
% relation BACKWARD (bind the word `laptop`, recall the two syllables that
% blend into it). A syllable pair this source does not demonstrate blending
% is not in the table, so a recall on it abstains honestly — the engine
% never invents a blend.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli syllable-blending.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "syllable-blending.adj"

? syllable_blending(lap, top, $Word)        % expect laptop
? syllable_blending($S1, $S2, laptop)       % expect lap, top — reverse recall
? syllable_blending(pea, nut, $Word)        % expect abstain — not the pair this source demonstrates
